{"type":"message","id":"d106801c","parentId":"a00ff108","timestamp":"2026-09-26T23:17:40.502Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-3820d48a-cf08-435d-b1ac-28ecafd0ffde","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Unified code search/read tool. Replaces grep/glob/find/cat with token-budget aware output.\n\nUsage: ffs [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]\n\nCommands:\n  find        Find files by name (replaces `find` and `fd`)\n  glob        Match files by glob pattern (replaces `glob` and shell `**`)\n  grep        Search file contents (replaces `grep` and `rg`)\n  multi-grep  Multi-pattern OR content search (Aho-Corasick; literal needles) [aliases: multigrep]\n  read        Read a file with token-budget aware truncation (replaces `cat`)\n  outline     Render a file's structural outline (functions, classes, …)\n  symbol      Look up symbol definitions (NEW; tree-sitter AST powered)\n  callers     List callers of a symbol (NEW)\n  callees     List callees referenced inside a symbol body (NEW)\n  refs        List definitions and usages of a symbol in one shot (NEW)\n  flow        Drill-down envelope per definition (def + body + callees + callers)\n  siblings    List sibling symbols (peers in the same parent scope)\n  deps        Show a file's imports + the workspace files that depend on it\n  impact      Rank files by how much they'd be affected if a symbol changed (NEW)\n  index       Build / refresh the on-disk indexes (Bigram, Bloom, Symbol, Outline)\n  map         Render the workspace as a tree annotated with file count and tokens\n  overview    High-signal summary of the workspace (languages, top symbols, …)\n  mcp         Run as MCP server over stdio (replaces agent built-ins Grep/Glob/Read)\n  mention     Resolve a @-mention payload (Phase C surface — wraps the Phase B `resolve_mentions` engine API; tokens in the input become substring candidate queries against the repo)\n  guide       Print the embedded agent guide\n  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nOptions:\n      --root <ROOT>                Root directory to search/index. Defaults to current working dir\n      --format <FORMAT>            Output format [default: text] [possible values: text, json]\n      --completions <COMPLETIONS>  Generate shell completions for the given shell [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]\n  -h, --help                       Print help\n  -V, --version                    Print version\n\n\nWall time: 0.11 seconds"}],"details":{"timeoutSeconds":60,"wallTimeMs":107.83707999996841},"isError":false,"timestamp":1790464660502}}
