ic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/Gitlawb-openclaude/src/utils/nativeInstaller/installer.ts:1561:   const configMap = getShellConfigPaths()\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/Gitlawb-openclaude/src/utils/nativeInstaller/installer.ts:1563:   for (const [shellType, configFile] of Object.entries(configMap)) {\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:1: # Design System: Figma\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:18: Figma's interface is the design tool that designed itself — a masterclass in typographic sophistication where a custom variable font (figmaSans) modulates between razor-thin (weight 320) and bold (weight 700) with stops at unusual intermediates (330, 340, 450, 480, 540) that most type systems never explore. This granular weight control gives every text element a precisely calibrated visual weight, creating hierarchy through micro-differences rather than the blunt instrument of \"regular vs bold.\"\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:20: The page presents a fascinating duality: the interface chrome is strictly black-and-white (literally only `#000000` and `#ffffff` detected as colors), while the hero section and product showcases explode with vibrant multi-color gradients — electric greens, bright yellows, deep purples, hot pinks. This separation means the design system itself is colorless, treating the product's colorful output as the hero content. Figma's marketing page is essentially a white gallery wall displaying colorful art.\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:22: What makes Figma distinctive beyond the variable font is its circle-and-pill geometry. Buttons use 50px radius (pill) or 50% (perfect circle for icon buttons), creating an organic, tool-palette-like feel. The dashed-outline focus indicator (`dashed 2px`) is a deliberate design choice that echoes selection handles in the Figma editor itself — the website's UI language references the product's UI language.\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:25: - Custom variable font (figmaSans) with unusual weight stops: 320, 330, 340, 450, 480, 540, 700\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:27: - figmaMono for uppercase technical labels with wide letter-spacing\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:29: - Dashed focus outlines echoing Figma's editor selection handles\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:40: *Note: Figma's marketing site uses ONLY these two colors for its interface layer. All vibrant colors appear exclusively in product screenshots, hero gradients, and embedded content.*\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:54: - **Primary**: `figmaSans`, with fallbacks: `figmaSans Fallback, SF Pro Display, system-ui, helvetica`\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:55: - **Monospace / Labels**: `figmaMono`, with fallbacks: `figmaMono Fallback, SF Mono, menlo`\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:61: | Display / Hero | figmaSans | 86px (5.38rem) | 400 | 1.00 (tight) | -1.72px | Maximum impact, extreme tracking |\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:62: | Section Heading | figmaSans | 64px (4rem) | 400 | 1.10 (tight) | -0.96px | Feature section titles |\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:63: | Sub-heading | figmaSans | 26px (1.63rem) | 540 | 1.35 | -0.26px | Emphasized section text |\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:64: | Sub-heading Light | figmaSans | 26px (1.63rem) | 340 | 1.35 | -0.26px | Light-weight section text |\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:65: | Feature Title | figmaSans | 24px (1.5rem) | 700 | 1.45 | normal | Bold card headings |\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:66: | Body Large | figmaSans | 20px (1.25rem) | 330–450 | 1.30–1.40 | -0.1px to -0.14px | Descriptions, intros |\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:67: | Body / Button | figmaSans | 16px (1rem) | 330–400 | 1.40–1.45 | -0.14px to normal | Standard body, nav, buttons |\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:68: | Body Light | figmaSans | 18px (1.13rem) | 320 | 1.45 | -0.26px to normal | Light-weight body text |\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:69: | Mono Label | figmaMono | 18px (1.13rem) | 400 | 1.30 (tight) | 0.54px | Uppercase section labels |\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:70: | Mono Small | figmaMono | 12px (0.75rem) | 400 | 1.00 (tight) | 0.6px | Uppercase tiny tags |\n/home/toxic/sovereign/projects/nim-repos/h0rcrux-hermes-backup/skills/creative/popular-web-designs/templates/figma.md:73: - **Variable font precision**: figma