{"type":"message","id":"592e1b1d","parentId":"f720d8de","timestamp":"2026-09-26T23:18:05.714Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-dd4ae6bb-e7df-4631-b2e9-28665a33cf21","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Search file contents (replaces `grep` and `rg`)\n\nUsage: ffs grep [OPTIONS] <NEEDLE>\n\nArguments:\n  <NEEDLE>  Pattern. Auto-detected as a regular expression when it contains any regex metacharacter (`.`, `*`, `+`, `?`, `^`, `$`, `[`, `(`, `|`, `\\`). Force literal interpretation with `--fixed-strings`, or force regex with `--regex`\n\nOptions:\n      --limit <LIMIT>\n          Maximum lines emitted total across all files [default: 200]\n      --root <ROOT>\n          Root directory to search/index. Defaults to current working dir\n      --format <FORMAT>\n          Output format [default: text] [possible values: text, json]\n      --offset <OFFSET>\n          Skip this many matches before starting the page. Use together with `--limit` to page past a truncated result set (see the `[N-M of total]` footer) [default: 0]\n      --completions <COMPLETIONS>\n          Generate shell completions for the given shell [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]\n  -s, --case-sensitive\n          Match case sensitively (default: false / smart-case when unset)\n  -i, --ignore-case\n          Match case insensitively, overriding smart-case (like `rg -i`)\n  -r, --regex\n          Force regex interpretation (overrides auto-detection)\n  -F, --fixed-strings\n          Force literal / fixed-string interpretation (overrides auto-detection)\n  -w, --word-regexp\n          Require whole-word matches (wraps the pattern with `\\b…\\b`)\n      --word-boundary <WORD_BOUNDARY>\n          Word-boundary definition for `-w` on the literal path: `unicode` (default, like `rg -w` — letters and digits are word chars) or `ascii` (ASCII letters/digits only). Regex-mode `-w` always uses the regex engine's own `\\b` [default: unicode] [possible values: unicode, ascii]\n  -v, --invert-match\n          Invert matching: select non-matching lines (like `rg -v`)\n      --max-count <MAX_COUNT>\n          Stop after N matches per file. 0 = unlimited (default) [default: 0]\n  -m, --max-count-per-file <MAX_COUNT_PER_FILE>\n          Shorthand for `--max-count 1` per file (like `rg -m 1`)\n  -l, --files-with-matches\n          Output only the file paths (one per line) — like `rg -l`\n      --files-without-match\n          Output only files with NO match (like `rg --files-without-match`)\n      --hidden\n          Search hidden files and directories (like `rg --hidden`)\n      --no-ignore\n          Don't respect `.gitignore` / `.ignore` files (like `rg --no-ignore`)\n  -a, --text\n          Search binary files as if they were text (like `rg -a/--text`)\n  -g, --glob <GLOBS>\n          Include files matching the given glob (repeatable, like `rg -g`). Example: `-g '*.rs' -g '!target/**'`\n  -o, --only-matching\n          Only show the matching part of each line (like `rg -o/--only-matching`)\n      --group\n          Group matches by file and enclosing symbol (like agentgrep)\n      --compact\n          Compact rg-like output: one `path:line:text` row per match, paths relative to the search root, no context lines or separators. Token-efficient for agents and pipes; implies relative paths. Explicit `-A`/`-B`/`-C` are ignored when set (use default output for context). `-l`/`--group` already emit compact shapes. Also applies to `-l`/`--files-without-match` path rows\n  -A, --after-context <AFTER_CONTEXT>\n          Lines of context to show after each match (like `rg -A`) [default: 0]\n  -B, --before-context <BEFORE_CONTEXT>\n          Lines of context to show before each match (like `rg -B`) [default: 0]\n  -C, --context <CONTEXT>\n          Lines of context to show before AND after each match (like `rg -C`). Overridden per-side by `--after-context`/`--before-context` if those are also given [default: 0]\n  -h, --help\n          Print help\n\nEXAMPLES:\n  ffs grep TODO                            # smart-case literal search\n  ffs grep '\\bTODO\\b' --regex            # forced regex (auto-detect would also pick this up)\n  ffs grep -F '.is_file()'                 # force literal — '.' won't be a regex wildcard\n  ffs grep --regex 'fn\\s+\\w+\\(' --root crates/  # signature-style regex over a sub-tree\n  ffs grep -w error                        # whole-word match only\n  ffs grep -l fixme                        # files-with-matches mode (one path per line)\n  ffs grep -C 2 handleSubmit                # 2 lines of context before/after each match\n  ffs grep TODO --offset 200                # page past the first 200 matches\n\n\nWall time: 0.11 seconds"}],"details":{"timeoutSeconds":60,"wallTimeMs":105.6547750000027},"isError":false,"timestamp":1790464685713}}
